<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan monopoly adjusts petrochemical prices.</title>
<headline>Taiwan monopoly adjusts petrochemical prices.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp said on Friday it had adjusted product prices for January.</p>
<p>Prices, announced at the end of a month, are valid until the end of the following month.</p>
<p>Prices are in U.S. dollars per tonne except where noted.</p>
<p> Product					     Jan   Dec</p>
<p> Ethylene					    587   554</p>
<p> Polymer grade propylene			 460   430</p>
<p> Chemical grade propylene			427   397</p>
<p> Butadiene					   480   457</p>
<p> Benzene					     322   308</p>
<p> Paraxylene					  468   423</p>
<p> Orthoxylene					 413   381</p>
<p> Carbon black feedstock (per kilolitre)    124   129</p>
<p>-- Taipei newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
